# Database
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-shm
# `-wal` plus fsqlite 0.2+'s `-wal-cert` / `-wal-cert-head` durability sidecars (br 0.7).
*.db-wal*
# fsqlite namespace sidecars — per-machine sqlite runtime state, written 0600 next to the DB
# (`beads.db-fsqlite-ns-use`, `-ns-gate`). Exactly the escape the #271 note below describes: the
# suffix clears `*.db-wal`/`*.db-shm`, and `*.db` only matches the bare filename, so both were
# left tracked. Verified with `git check-ignore` — without this, the first `git add .beads`
# commits one machine's DB state into a shared repo.
*.db-fsqlite-*
# Vacuum sidecars: `.beads.vacuum.<pid>.tmp-fsqlite-ns-{use,gate}`. The SAME suffix escape as
# above, one step further out — `*.db-fsqlite-*` wants `.db-` and these carry `.tmp-`, while
# `*.tmp` only matches a trailing `.tmp`, so both globs miss and the pair lands untracked next
# to the DB. That is how one machine's vacuum state got committed in #1474 by a `git add -A`.
*.tmp-fsqlite-*
# br 0.7 (fsqlite 0.3), matching br's own BEADS_GITIGNORE. The vacuum copies
# `br doctor migrate-schema apply` leaves as
# `.beads.db.schema-migration-<run>.vacuum-{fsqlite-ns-gate,fsqlite-ns-use,wal-cert,wal-cert-head}`
# carry `.vacuum-` where the globs above want `.db-` or `.tmp-` — the same suffix
# escape, a third time — so the namespace sidecars are matched by their tail.
*-fsqlite-ns-gate
*-fsqlite-ns-use
*.vacuum-wal-cert*
# fsqlite 0.3.6+ engine-upgrade bookkeeping, beside the DB and its vacuum copy.
*.fsqlite-migration-state
# WAL-index quarantines br 0.7 leaves beside the database
# (`.br-wal-index-<random>/`). Not in br's canonical list; found on disk.
.br-wal-index-*/

# Lock files — `*.lock` also covers br 0.7's `.br-db-openers-<h>.lock`,
# `.br-db-write-<h>.lock`, `.br-jsonl-write-<h>.lock` and `*.transition.lock`.
.write.lock
.write-waiters.lock/
*.lock

# Temporary
last-touched
*.tmp

# Local history backups
.br_history/

# DB-family recovery artifacts (truncated WAL/SHM, quarantined sidecars)
# — same lifecycle as .br_history/, written by recovery paths and
# `br doctor --repair`. Filename suffix `.truncated-wal` slips past the
# generic `*.db-wal` glob above, so it needs an explicit entry (#271).
.br_recovery/

# Sync state (local-only, per-machine)
.sync.lock
sync_base.jsonl

# Merge artifacts (temporary files from 3-way merge)
beads.base.jsonl
beads.base.meta.json
beads.left.jsonl
beads.left.meta.json
beads.right.jsonl
beads.right.meta.json

# Daemon runtime files
daemon.lock
daemon.log
daemon.pid
bd.sock
sync-state.json

# Worktree redirect file
redirect

# bv (beads viewer) lock file
.bv.lock
